<title>AUSTRALIA: Coal &amp; Allied says coal strike over.</title>
<headline>Coal &amp; Allied says coal strike over.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Striking coal miners voted on Tuesday morning to return to work at Rio Tinto Ltd unit Coal and Allied Ltd's Hunter Valley mine north of Sydney.</p>
<p>The decision ended a six-week strike which Coal and Allied estimated had cost the company A$1 million a day in lost revenue.</p>
<p>The workers, members of the Construction, Forestry Mining and Energy Union, voted 80 opercent to 20 percent to return to work from midnight on Tuesday, Allan Davies, general manager of the Hunter Valley Number One coal mine, told Reuters.  </p>
<p>The first train was expected to be moving with coal by about 10.45 am (2445 GMT) Tuesday. First shipments are expected to leave the port in about two days time.</p>
<p>Early shipments are scheduled for Korea and Italy.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
